preConditionHook:
// The EL twin's windowed maximum of the bar range over the runBars bars
// ENDING ONE BAR AGO, so the current bar is not its own competitor. Written as
// the Extremes loop it bottoms out in -- seeded at the first candidate (bar 1),
// scanning the rest with a STRICT comparison so a tie keeps the earliest bar --
// rather than as a history reference on a function call. Extremes is EL SOURCE,
// so its comparison carries the ordinary relational tolerance and uses el_gt.
// The operands are differences of two tick-grid prices, where that tolerance is
// inert either way.
maxRange = high[1] - low[1];
for (ii = 2; ii <= (int)runBars; ++ii) {
    if (el_gt(high[ii] - low[ii], maxRange)) maxRange = high[ii] - low[ii];
}
